            Events on coverage names (discovery funnel stage 4): the deterministic "something happened to a name we cover" handler.
            For each hit a detector noted on a coverage member, once ever per (ticker, source, reference):


records it as a  (the digest's rows) and moves the member's LastEventAt to now;

re-scores the member's Active candidate (, the score_candidate path: market structure and fundamentals read, no model);

runs the stage 1 remove rules on the member (, which reads , so a removal journals the rule that fired and the removal cutoff applies on the way back in);

writes the outcome back on the event row.

            The review-due notice (CandidateReviewDue / ThesisReviewDue) is raised by the detector through
            , once per subject, source and reference; the hit carries the notice it raised, which this class
            records on the event. A repeat of a recorded hit returns before touching anything, so a detector that re-reads the same filing or
            the same day's cluster every run costs one lookup. No model is called anywhere here.

